{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Access Control - Network Zones - Okta Network Zone Modified or Unblocked",
	"Description": "A network zone was modified, or an address range was removed from a blocklist zone. Adding the adversary's own egress range to a trusted zone, or pulling it out of a blocklist, turns a location restriction into a no-op.\n\nEvent types: zone.update, zone.remove_blacklist, security.zone.remove_blacklist\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/defense_evasion_okta_attempt_to_modify_okta_network_zone/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "2f7507c8-0f89-5bd7-939c-b1b0f84c083f",
	"SearchReference": "f7dc12d0-81b4-5564-bb84-f4538c01d027"
